# Fixture manifests hash LF bytes. Keep text identical on Windows and Unix.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.pptx binary
*.zip binary

# Stronger rule for fixtures: `text=auto` lets git GUESS which files are text,
# so an unlisted extension can still get its line endings rewritten — and every
# byte under fixtures/ is sha256-verified against manifest.csv. Checked out
# verbatim, no guessing, no conversion.
#
# Concretely: fixtures/t02_raw_qc/images.csv has 97 lines, so a CRLF checkout
# makes it 97 bytes longer, the sha256 no longer matches, verify_manifest fails
# and strict_provenance aborts src.main with exit 2.
fixtures/** -text
